### Open finding (pre-existing, not from this work)
`test_registration_guard.sh` FAILS: the BUILT vsim engines' `config.inc` now
hash to `3916affd` (premium) / `5ba65369` (advanced), but the registration dirs
are `-ed1cb158` / `-4d194785`. The vsim was rebuilt with a different config
since registration; `config.inc` carries no volatile content (hash is stable),
so this is a genuine config change, not hash noise. Re-registration (rename dirs
to the new hash + regenerate manifests) is the bring-up flow -- and it is exactly
where F3's probe pays off, because `gen_manifest.py`'s hand-traced `P` params
(line 30) do not auto-adapt to a rebuilt config. The F1/F2 gates still pass
because the transported CSR set is compatible, but the manifests are stale vs
the current build. Left as a reported finding, NOT silently re-registered (that
would claim registration for a config not re-audited).
